{{!--
  The lead. What happened, who it affected, why, and where it stands — before
  any chart. A reader who stops after this block should still know whether the
  month was fine.

  `rows` is [{label, value}, ...]. Deliberately unopinionated about which rows
  appear: the right ones depend on what the data actually says. The bundled
  `buildIncidentBrief` view builder derives them from the aggregation and
  omits the brief entirely when the month recorded no events.

  Values are plain text and stay double-braced: issue summaries and channel
  names come from parsed log content, which is untrusted. A row that needs
  markup should be a separate partial, not an unescaped value here.
--}}
<section class="incident-brief" aria-labelledby="incident-brief-heading">
  {{#if eyebrow}}<p class="incident-brief__eyebrow">{{eyebrow}}</p>{{/if}}
  {{#if headline}}<h2 class="incident-brief__headline" id="incident-brief-heading">{{headline}}</h2>{{/if}}
  {{#each rows}}
  <div class="incident-brief__row">
    <div class="incident-brief__label">{{this.label}}</div>
    <div class="incident-brief__value">{{this.value}}</div>
  </div>
  {{/each}}
</section>
